WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.156
Vesicles are cavities made by gas bubbles in lava. As pressure

00:00:04.156 --> 00:00:07.961
falls, dissolved gas comes out of solution and bubbles begin to

00:00:07.961 --> 00:00:08.307
grow.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.022
The review compares pumice and scoria. Pumice commonly has many thin-walled

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:21.695
cavities and can float. Scoria commonly has darker, thicker walls. Their

00:00:21.695 --> 00:00:22.544
compositions differ.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.899
Cooling preserves the bubbles as holes. These are vesicles, not crystals.
